4. TIPPERS — THE HIDDEN PRODUCTIVITY DRIVER
This is extremely important for your future P&M Head/AGM interview.

A road project can have excellent excavators, crushers and HMPs but still lose production because of insufficient tippers.
Example
Suppose:
- HMP = 160 TPH
- One tipper carries = 20 T
- Loading = 5 min
- Travel loaded = 25 min
- Unloading = 3 min
- Return = 20 min
- Waiting = 5 min
Total cycle ≈ 58 min

One tipper:

20 × 60 / 58 ≈ 20.7 TPH

For 160 TPH:

160 / 20.7 ≈ 7.7

So you need approximately 8 productive tippers, plus contingency.

But if traffic, haul distance or loading delays increase, the requirement increases.
This is why P&M should calculate:
Required Tippers = Plant Output × Haul Cycle / Truck Payload / 60

This principle applies to:
- Crusher → WMM
- Quarry → WMM
- HMP → Paver
- Excavation → Embankment
- RMC → Structure
